  "note": "Cross-repository pin for the per-row trading-cost model. Stock-Grader (src/stock_grader/costs.py) and Stock-Vault (src/stock_vault/costs.py) implement this model independently because neither repository may import the other; this file is what keeps the two implementations from drifting apart in silence. Both repositories carry a byte-identical copy and both assert its sha256. `vectors` pins the COMPOSITION (liquidity inputs in, one cost estimate out); `bar_vectors` pins the ESTIMATORS themselves (raw daily bars in, spread/sigma/lambda out), which the composition vectors cannot reach because they take the spread as a scalar input. Every input below is a synthetic round number chosen for arithmetic convenience: nothing here is measured from any archive, so the file is safe in a public repository. Tolerance: relative 1e-9. A change to this file is a change to the cost model and must land in both repositories in the same breath.",
